# Coding standards

- TypeScript only in app code. No `any`; narrow `unknown`.
- `'use client'` only for browser/Yjs/interactive UI.
- Functional components. Collaboration (Y.Doc, provider, awareness) lives in hooks or `lib/collab`, not presentational components.
- Permission helpers: `canView`, `canComment`, `canEdit`. Use them in routes and UI.
- Handle errors at route and WebSocket boundaries. No empty `catch`.
- Do not log tokens or private document text.
- Disable the editor for `view` and `comment` roles; comments allowed for `comment` and `edit`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
await prisma.page.update({ where: { id }, data: { contentHtml: html } });

// ✅ GOOD
await persistYjsUpdate({ pageId: id, update, userId });
```
